The control confirms deterministic starvation beyond the stated limit: with SQS calls at 50 seconds and DynamoDB calls at 30 seconds, both receive orders leave all four jobs unfilled across 12 polls. One receive plus complete handling and acknowledgement succeeds in 250 seconds at the same budget. DESIGN.md mentions probabilistic fairness and capacity, but its “starvation-free” claim misses this case. The adapted original probes all collect the signatures.

I also missed redirecting pytest’s temporary fixtures: the suite used its default `/tmp/pytest-of-tony`, outside the requested scratch directory. Repository bytecode and pytest cache writes were disabled.
